# 74. Final Rule for Future Development

Before changing the data model or making assumptions about Scaler's APIs, refer to this document.

Separate facts into:

```text
OBSERVED
```

versus:

```text
ASSUMED / NOT YET VERIFIED
```

Do not turn an assumption into production logic merely because one endpoint happened to behave a certain way once.

The strongest verified foundation is:

```text
test ID
    ↓
GET /api/v2/tests/{test_id}/problems
    ↓
problem ID
    ↓
GET /api/v2/tests/{test_id}/problems/{problem_id}/user_submissions
    ↓
submission.created_at
submission.status
    ↓
historical solved date
```

Everything above this layer — especially automatic discovery of all historical tests — is the next problem to solve.
